{
  "name": "W1 \u00b7 Enquiry intake and triage \u2014 Photo & video studio",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## W1 \u2014 Enquiry intake \u00b7 Photo & video studio\n\n**Boundary decision: fully automated.**\nVariance low-ish, consequence low (a misfiling surfaces in the queue), input short. Scored 2/1/2 on variance / consequence / data-availability.\n\n**Except one case.** An emergency must leave the automated path immediately. That branch is the red note below \u2014 if it ever stops working, that is not a bug report, it is a finding for your results chapter.\n\n### Before you run this\n1. Open **Extract enquiry fields** and pick your Anthropic credential.\n2. Open the three **Google Sheets** nodes and set the document ID.\n3. Replace `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_SPREADSHEET_ID` throughout.\n\n### Test it\nPaste each record from this pack's `enquiries.json` into the form. Every file has a record that must be refused, one that must escalate, and one out-of-area case \u2014 each says so in its `notes_for_testing`.\n\n### What is different about this industry\nAvailability is a hard binary on a named date rather than a scheduling puzzle - a second wedding on an already booked Saturday cannot be solved with a better price, a longer lead time or a bigger crew, which is the one failure mode no amount of quoting intelligence can rescue. The deliverable is creative and taste-dependent, so qualification depends on judgements about style fit that do not reduce to structured fields, and a mismatched booking is a worse outcome than a lost one. And the price hinges on usage rights the enquirer usually does not think to mention - the customer asking for 'just a few product photos' for a national campaign is the same sentence as the customer wanting them for an Instagram post, with an order of magnitude between the two proposals.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 560,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "b221e419-2ff4-4d41-b282-abbf122c5d8a",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -820,
        -420
      ]
    },
