        }
      },
      "id": "e66efcf0-87a7-4a8c-81aa-6d9770a10626",
      "name": "Enquiry form",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -260,
        -180
      ],
      "webhookId": "5401c887-8e01-4693-836a-76ddc1771a6a"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One shape for every channel. The form is only one door \u2014 email, SMS and phone\n// transcripts arrive via other triggers and are normalised to exactly this object,\n// so everything downstream reads the same fields regardless of where it came from.\n//\n// `raw` is never overwritten anywhere in the pipeline. Extraction can then be re-run\n// and compared later, which is what makes the prompt-version comparison possible.\nconst now = new Date().toISOString();\n\nreturn items.map((item, i) => {\n  const f = item.json;\n  return {\n    json: {\n      job_id: `JOB-${new Date().getFullYear()}-${String(Date.now()).slice(-4)}${i}`,\n      state: 'new',\n      created_at: now,\n      channel: f.channel ?? 'web-form',\n      raw: f.raw ?? '',\n      form_customer_name: f.customer_name ?? null,\n      form_email: f.email ?? null,\n      form_phone: f.phone ?? null,\n      form_address: f.address ?? null,\n      events: [],\n    },\n  };\n});"
      },
      "id": "223b7e15-4813-41b8-bf9b-530e0a1ce5cd",
      "name": "Normalise inbound",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "text": "={{ $json.raw }}",
        "schemaType": "manual",
        "inputSchema": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"customer_name\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"email\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"phone\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"locality\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"language\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"de\",\n        \"en\",\n        \"fr\",\n        \"it\",\n        \"unknown\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"job_type\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"described_scope\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"urgency\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"emergency\",\n        \"urgent\",\n        \"scheduled\",\n        \"no_rush\",\n        \"unknown\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"deadline\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"in_service_area\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"boolean\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"is_repeat_customer\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"missing_fields\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"extraction_confidence\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"disqualify_reason\": {\n      \"type\": [\n        \"string\",\n        \"null\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"language\",\n    \"urgency\",\n    \"missing_fields\",\n    \"extraction_confidence\"\n  ]\n}",
        "options": {
          "systemPromptTemplate": "You extract structured data from enquiry messages sent to a small photography and video studio in canton St. Gallen, Switzerland. They arrive in German or English and are often incomplete.\n\nNever invent a value. If a field is not present, return null and name it in missing_fields. A plausible guess is worse than a null: a null gets asked about, a guess gets acted on.\n\nKeep described_scope in the language it was written in and set language accordingly.\n\nurgency is about consequence, not tone. A calm message can describe an emergency and an angry one can describe something trivial. For this business, treat as an emergency: Genuinely time-critical means the date cannot be moved and the window closes within days: a wedding or a one-off event happening this week, a photographer or videographer dropping out of a booked date, or a client's campaign, print run or trade-fair stand that has a fixed delivery deadline already committed to a third party. A wedding is the sharpest form of this constraint, because the date is fixed by the couple and the venue and cannot be rescheduled to suit availability, so a late enquiry is either accepted now or lost entirely. Anything in this class must escalate to a human immediately, because the only useful answer is a yes or no on availability from someone who can actually commit the diary.\n\nService area \u2014 Distance is a pricing input here, not a qualifier: travel time, a travel day and accommodation are billable line items, and destination work is normal and often welcome, so an enquiry from outside the area should be priced with travel added rather than declined the way a trade contractor would decline it.\nIn: St. Gallen, Gossau, Wittenbach, Rorschach, Arbon, Herisau, Teufen, Flawil. Out: Zermatt, Lugano, Geneva, Zurich Airport. If a locality is stated but you do not recognise it, return null rather than guessing \u2014 a wrong false loses real work.\n\nextraction_confidence is your honest estimate that a human reading the same text would extract the same fields. Do not inflate it.\n\nIf no actionable shoot is described at all, set job_type null and give a disqualify_reason."
        }
      },
      "id": "034936ac-2aab-4280-b0dc-92bc4d88cd4b",
      "name": "Extract enquiry fields",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.informationExtractor",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        220,
        -180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929"
        },
