    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The escalation branch\n\nThis is the only unconditional exit from the automated path in W1.\n\nGenuinely time-critical means the date cannot be moved and the window closes within days: a wedding or a one-off event happening this week, a photographer or videographer dropping out of a booked date, or a client's campaign, print run or trade-fair stand that has a fixed delivery deadline already committed to a third party. A wedding is the sharpest form of this constraint, because the date is fixed by the couple and the venue and cannot be rescheduled to suit availability, so a late enquiry is either accepted now or lost entirely. Anything in this class must escalate to a human immediately, because the only useful answer is a yes or no on availability from someone who can actually commit the diary.\n\nNone of that belongs in a pricing pipeline. If your triage ever routes one into the normal flow, **report it** \u2014 an automation that handles an emergency as routine admin is exactly the kind of boundary failure this thesis is about.",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 240,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "8fb56f83-58b0-4587-baa7-9f129685664e",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        940,
        -480
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "send",
        "fromEmail": "workflow@example.ch",
        "toEmail": "owner@example.ch",
        "subject": "=URGENT \u2014 {{ $json.customer_name || 'unknown contact' }} \u2014 call now",
        "emailFormat": "html",
        "html": "=<p><strong>Possible emergency. Automated handling stopped.</strong></p><p><strong>Contact:</strong> {{ $json.phone || $json.email || 'NONE SUPPLIED' }}</p><p><strong>They wrote:</strong></p><blockquote>{{ $json.raw }}</blockquote><p>Record {{ $json.job_id }} received {{ $json.created_at }}.</p>",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "0df31c6d-dc01-4db4-9ae7-ddcea8166630",
      "name": "Alert owner immediately",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.emailSend",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        960,
